This README is designed specifically for the modular, improved version of your ASL project. It explains the new features, the file structure, and how they work together to create a professional fingerspelling tool.

ASL Fingerspelling Pro 🤟
This is an enhanced, modular version of the ASL Class Thinkers recognition system. While the original project laid the groundwork, this version is specifically optimized for Static Alphabet Recognition (A-Z) and Real-time Fingerspelling Translation.

🌟 Key Improvements
Stability Buffer (Anti-Flicker): Implemented a frame-buffer logic that prevents "jittery" predictions. A letter is only captured once the hand position remains stable for 10 consecutive frames.

Sentence Builder: Added a persistent history state allowing users to chain letters together into words and sentences.

Smart Confusion Logic: Integrated a custom calibration layer to handle common ASL "look-alikes" (e.g., distinguishing between M, N, S, and A).

Text-to-Speech (TTS): Integrated the Web Speech API so the application can "speak" the transcribed fingerspelling aloud.

Enhanced Preprocessing: Added CLAHE (Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization) to the hand-detection pipeline to improve accuracy in low-light environments.

📁 Modular File Structure
To make the code cleaner and easier to maintain, the project has been split into functional modules:

File	Purpose
app.py	The main entry point and UI controller.
config.py	Global settings, confusion pairs, and page configurations.
asl_engine.py	The "brain"—handles stability logic and history management.
hand_detector.py	Manages MediaPipe tracking and image enhancement (CLAHE).
ui_components.py	Contains reusable UI elements like the Reference Gallery and TTS button.


🛠️ Installation & Setup
Clone the updated repository:

Bash

git clone https://github.com/ali-ezz/ASL_CLASS_THINKERS.git
cd ASL_CLASS_THINKERS
Install the required dependencies:

Bash

pip install streamlit opencv-python mediapipe numpy streamlit-webrtc
Run the application:

Bash

streamlit run app.py
📖 How to Use
Launch the App: Open the Streamlit URL in your browser.

Position Hand: Place your hand in the camera view. The system will detect your hand and draw a bounding box.

Hold for 1 Second: To "type" a letter, hold the sign steady. Once the STABLE indicator appears, the letter is added to your word.

Edit your Word: Use the Backspace or Clear buttons to refine your sentence.

Listen: Click the 🔊 Speak button to hear the final transcription.

